  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When existing content is loaded into the Unity 2018-based versions of VRC, materials with a HDR colour will appear incorrect, due to Unity changing how HDR colour values are interpreted. A tool to fix this is now provided in the SDK. \nBut for content already uploaded with no other issues, this means updating Unity, resolving new issues caused by the update, and rebuilding data that the Unity editor is no longer compatible with (i.e. LightingData). This is no small task, and a sizeable time investment. \nIt would save a lot of effort if VRC's client modified older content when loading to either apply the gamma transform to the colours of materials, or apply the gamma flag to the material properties.",
